// Find the Path: `BuffKind::Detecting` applied to `SenseKind::Path`, the one
// sense kind that reveals a place instead of a set of things
// (`server/src/sys/detection.rs`'s `evaluate_sense`): it resolves to the
// nearest `WaypointArea` entity in range and surfaces it as a single
// `DetectedPoint`, rendered through the in-world label surface rather than
// the minimap. This maps directly onto the real, already-wired
// `WaypointArea` component campfires and similar rest points carry -- no
// simplification of the underlying mechanism needed, only of scope: the
// D&D original finds a route to any destination the caster has ever known,
// which has no literal engine equivalent, so this finds the nearest actual
// waypoint entity instead.
//
// Radius: 450 m, the same "wide area" tier `commune_with_nature.ron` uses,
// reflecting this spell's own high level (6th) and the flavour of finding a
// route across real distance -- a deliberately bounded substitute for the
// D&D original's effectively unlimited pathfinding.
//
// `SenseMode::Snapshot`: the nearest waypoint is resolved once at cast and
// held for the buff's `Concentration(60)` duration, matching "the sense of
// the way persists... as long as you keep your attention fixed upon it."
SelfBuff(
    buildup_duration: 0.5,
    cast_duration: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.3,
    buffs: [
        BuffDesc(
            kind: Detecting,
            data: BuffData(
                strength: 0.0,
                duration: Some(60.0),
                misc_data: Some(Sense(Path, 450.0, Snapshot)),
            ),
        ),
    ],
    energy_cost: 50,
    enforced_limit: false,
    meta: (
        school: Some(Divination),
        source: Some(Divine),
        // level 6 spell -> min_level 36, same `level * 6` convention
        // see_invisibility.ron/true_seeing.ron derive from every other
        // shipped spell that sets this field.
        requirements: (min_level: Some(36)),
    ),
)
